module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraSheafModuleFunctor.Subobject
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiCompactColimit.AffineCover
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionEpiAffine.AlgebraSheaf

/-!
# Finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras cut out by a locally surjective map

Let `X` be a scheme and `A` a sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras.  The colimit assertion of
[Stacks, Tag 05JT] is reduced by
`Stacks.QuasiCompactColimit.nonempty_isColimit_of_sections_of_mono` to one statement about
sections: over every affine open `U`, every `x ∈ A(U)` comes from a finite type quasi-coherent
subalgebra of `A`.  This file supplies the two steps of that statement which are *formal* in the
subalgebra, i.e. which hold for any scheme and ask nothing of `X`:

* a subalgebra of `A` which receives a locally surjective map from a finite type quasi-coherent
  algebra sheaf is itself of finite type, and
* such a subalgebra, together with a section of the finite type algebra lying over `x`, produces
  the object of `FiniteTypeSubalgebra A` and the section over `U` that the reduction asks for.

and it records, with a proof, what those two steps reduce the colimit assertion to.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebras.isFiniteType_of_isLocallySurjective`: **a
  locally surjective image of a finite type quasi-coherent algebra sheaf is of finite type.**
  Over an affine open the map on sections is surjective by
  `Stacks.SectionEpiAffine.surjective_sections_of_isLocallySurjective`, and a surjection out of
  a finite type algebra is of finite type.
* `exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_factorisation`, in the same namespace:
  a factorisation `C ⟶ B ⟶ A` of a section-producing map, with the first map locally surjective
  and the second a monomorphism, produces an object of `FiniteTypeSubalgebra A` together with a
  section over `U` mapping to the given `x`.
* `nonempty_isColimit_finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone_of_affineSections`, in the same namespace:
  **the colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 05JT], granted filteredness and the affine sections
  statement.**  So the colimit assertion takes three lines once the sections statement is
  available.

## Implementation notes

The structure morphism of the target of a morphism `e : C ⟶ B` under `X.sheaf` is
`C.hom ≫ e.right` by `CategoryTheory.Under.w`, so over an affine open the structure map of `B`
*is* the structure map of `C` followed by the map on sections; `RingHom.FiniteType.comp_surjective`
then applies, exactly as in `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebras.isFiniteType_of_iso`.

The section over `U` of the subobject `CategoryTheory.Subobject.mk i` is obtained by transporting
along `CategoryTheory.Subobject.underlyingIso i`, whose defining property
`CategoryTheory.Subobject.underlyingIso_arrow` is turned into a statement about sections by
`congrArg` at the fixed open and `CategoryTheory.ConcreteCategory.congr_hom` at the element.
`CategoryTheory.ConcreteCategory.comp_apply` must *not* be used to split the composite first:
here `rw` fails to find its pattern in a term of exactly that shape, while the
composite applied to an element is already definitionally the iterated application.

`CategoryTheory.Mono ((finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone A).ι.app B)` is **not** found by instance
search, even though the component is `B.obj.arrow` by `rfl`: the head of the goal is the cocone
projection and instance search does not unfold it.  A `show Mono B.obj.arrow from inferInstance`
is needed, where the identification is checked at the transparency of term elaboration.

## What this file does not contain, and where the rest of the tag is

**The sections statement is not proved here.** It is

```
theorem exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section
    {X : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (A : Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf X) (hA : A.IsQuasicoherent)
    (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (x : A.right.obj.obj (op U)) :
    ∃ (B : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A)
      (y : (B.obj : Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U)),
        (B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U)) y = x
```

and it is proved, in that generality, as
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section`. This
is where the quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of `X` enter: the subalgebra it asks for
is *global*, while `x` is given only over `U`. Its route is [Stacks, Tag 01PG] for modules, which
supplies a finite type quasi-coherent submodule `N` of the underlying module of `A` on the whole
of `X` with `x` among its sections over `U`, and then the subalgebra generated by `N`,
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.genSubalg`.

Three declarations this route relies on are available in the library, and are named here
because they are easy to overlook.

* Local surjectivity of the corestriction to the image, and quasi-coherence of the image, are
  `Stacks.AlgebraImageSurjective.imageIsLocallySurjective` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraImageSurjective.imageIsQuasicoherent`. Both are used together in the
  proof of `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag05JTColimitGlobal.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_top`
  (`ColimitGlobal/Basic.lean`), which meets the hypotheses of
  `exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_factorisation` below with an image.
* [Stacks, Tag 01PG] for modules is formalized: its colimit assertion is
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PGColimitClose.isColimit_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone`,
  whose affine sections half is
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PGColimitClose.affineSections_of_qcqs`, and its directedness
  assertion is `AlgebraicGeometry.finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_isFiltered`. The finite type
  quasi-coherent submodule in the form the subalgebra construction consumes is
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.exists_submodule_mem_of_qcqs`. Turning
  that submodule into an *algebra* needs no symmetric algebra: the subalgebra generated by it
  does.
* Filteredness of `FiniteTypeSubalgebra A` is
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra`,
  unconditional in `X` and carrying `@[stacks 05JT "directedness"]`. That is why
  `nonempty_isColimit_finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone_of_affineSections` below takes `IsFiltered` as
  an instance hypothesis rather than proving it: the instance is supplied at the call site.

**No stacks attribute is attached in this file**, and none is earned: each statement below
carries hypotheses the tags do not. Both assertions of [Stacks, Tag 05JT] are in
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered`, and both assertions of part (1) of
[Stacks, Tag 0817] are in `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteSubalgebras`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05JT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05JT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0817](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0817)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PG)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open Stacks.RelativeSpec

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebras

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **A locally surjective image of a finite type quasi-coherent algebra sheaf is of finite
type.**  If `e : C ⟶ B` is a morphism of quasi-coherent algebra sheaves whose underlying
morphism of sheaves of commutative rings is locally surjective and `C` is of finite type, then
`B` is of finite type: over an affine open the map on sections is surjective, and the structure
map of `B` is the structure map of `C` followed by it.

No hypothesis on `X` is used; the only quasi-compactness involved is that of the affine open at
which finite typeness is tested, inside
`Stacks.SectionEpiAffine.surjective_sections_of_isLocallySurjective`. -/
theorem isFiniteType_of_isLocallySurjective {B C : AlgebraSheaf X} (e : C ⟶ B)
    (hC : C.IsQuasicoherent) (hB : B.IsQuasicoherent)
    (he : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective e.right) (hCft : C.IsFiniteType) : B.IsFiniteType := by
  intro U hU
  have hsurj :=
    Stacks.SectionEpiAffine.surjective_sections_of_isLocallySurjective e hC hB he U hU
  have hw : C.hom ≫ e.right = B.hom := Under.w e
  have happ : (B.hom.hom.app (op U)).hom =
      (e.right.hom.app (op U)).hom.comp (C.hom.hom.app (op U)).hom := by
    rw [← hw]; rfl
  rw [happ]
  exact (hCft U hU).comp_surjective hsurj

/-- **A section of `A` over `U` which comes from a finite type quasi-coherent algebra sheaf
through a subalgebra comes from an object of `FiniteTypeSubalgebra A`.**  The data is a
monomorphism `i : B ⟶ A` with `B` quasi-coherent, a locally surjective `e : C ⟶ B` out of a
quasi-coherent algebra sheaf of finite type, and a section `c` of `C` over `U` mapping to `x`.

This is the formal half of the sections statement that the colimit assertion of
[Stacks, Tag 05JT] is reduced to: it converts a factorisation of a map producing `x` into the
subobject and the section that
`Stacks.QuasiCompactColimit.nonempty_isColimit_of_sections_of_mono` consumes.  `U` need not be
affine and `A` need not be quasi-coherent.  What it does not supply is the factorisation; for a
global section the factorisation through an image is supplied by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag05JTColimitGlobal.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_top`. -/
theorem exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_factorisation {A B C : AlgebraSheaf X}
    (i : B ⟶ A) [Mono i] (e : C ⟶ B)
    (hB : B.IsQuasicoherent) (hC : C.IsQuasicoherent) (hCft : C.IsFiniteType)
    (he : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective e.right)
    (U : X.Opens) (x : A.right.obj.obj (op U)) (c : C.right.obj.obj (op U))
    (hc : (e ≫ i).right.hom.app (op U) c = x) :
    ∃ (D : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A) (y : (D.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U)),
      (D.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U)) y = x := by
  refine ⟨ofMono i hB (isFiniteType_of_isLocallySurjective e hC hB he hCft),
    (Subobject.underlyingIso i).inv.right.hom.app (op U) (e.right.hom.app (op U) c), ?_⟩
  have key := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (congrArg (fun f : B ⟶ A => f.right.hom.app (op U))
      (Subobject.underlyingIso_arrow i)) (e.right.hom.app (op U) c)
  exact key.trans hc

/-- **The colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 05JT], granted filteredness and the affine sections
statement.**  If the finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A` form a filtered category and
every section of `A` over every affine open comes from one of them, then the canonical cocone
`finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone A` is colimiting.

Both hypotheses are discharged at the call site in
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered`; see the module documentation.  The
content is
`Stacks.QuasiCompactColimit.nonempty_isColimit_of_sections_of_mono`, whose injectivity half is
discharged from the monomorphisms of the subobject arrows; the sections hypothesis is the
statement of that theorem verbatim, the two spellings agreeing by `rfl` through
`Stacks.QuasiCompactColimit.algebraSectionsFunctor`. -/
theorem nonempty_isColimit_finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone_of_affineSections (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    [IsFiltered (FiniteTypeSubalgebra A)]
    (h : ∀ U : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen U → ∀ x : A.right.obj.obj (op U),
      ∃ (B : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A) (y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U)),
        (B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U)) y = x) :
    Nonempty (IsColimit (finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone A)) :=
  Stacks.QuasiCompactColimit.nonempty_isColimit_of_sections_of_mono _
    (fun B => show Mono B.obj.arrow from inferInstance) fun U hU x => h U hU x

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebras

end
